 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two jobs are named for these diodes: setting a reference voltage in a regulated power supply, and clamping to protect a circuit against overvoltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Range and test current",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Thirty-eight types span 2.0 V to 75 V nominal, each with its own two-character marking. Types up to MM3Z24 are tested at IZT = 5 mA; MM3Z27 and above at 2 mA. The knee impedance ZZK is given at IZK = 0.5 mA, except MM3Z2V0 at 1.0 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Dissipation is 200 mW up to Ta = 25 °C and falls in a straight line to zero at 150 °C. Typical junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 417 °C/W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature coefficient",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "From MM3Z2V0 to MM3Z4V3 both typical limits are at or below zero; MM3Z4V7, MM3Z5V1 and MM3Z5V6 span zero; from MM3Z6V2 upward both limits are positive, reaching 73.4 to 88.6 mV/°C for MM3Z75."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and handling",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moisture sensitivity level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free reflow peak of 260 °C. The mould compound is rated UL 94V-0 and is RoHS compliant and halogen free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. A stripe on the body marks the cathode."
  }
 ],
